# Villa Kiosk — environment defaults
# Copy to ".env" and fill in. All values are OPTIONAL: anything left blank can
# be entered at runtime in the Onboarding wizard / Settings.
#
# The HA URL/token are NOT env-configurable (there used to be a VITE_HA_URL/
# VITE_HA_TOKEN pair here) — a build-time default gets baked as plain text
# into the compiled JS bundle, and for a standalone deploy that's a public
# static file. A real long-lived token ending up there is a live credential
# leak to anyone who can fetch that file (see the incident this repo's
# CHANGELOG records), not just a convenience shortcut. Enter the URL/token
# once per physical device via the Onboarding wizard instead.

# --- Villa location for sun tracking (Bali / TheLysHouse) ---
VITE_LAT=-8.3405
VITE_LNG=115.0920

# --- Profile passcodes (standalone mode only) ---
# 4 digits each; leave empty (or unset) to let that profile in without a code.
# NOTE: Vite bakes these into the client bundle — treat them as a courtesy gate
# for a trusted kiosk device. In add-on mode, set the PINs in the add-on
# options instead (guest_pin / owner_pin / ops_pin) — those are verified
# server-side and never reach the browser.
# VITE_GUEST_PIN=
# VITE_OWNER_PIN=
# VITE_OPS_PIN=
